    '|a||So this monopoly costs not three hundred and twenty dollars a day, but up to nine hundred and sixty: triangle plus rectangle, three times Harberger''s count.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 9720
      voice: 'gemini:Achird | curious, open-minded economist host who loves a puzzle; warm, thinks aloud, brisk lively pace (never slow, never rushed); takes objections seriously, never preachy #ctx:1vuw3so'
    '|b||Tullock''s paper made the same point about theft. The stolen money only moves; the burglar''s time and your new locks are pure waste.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 8640
      voice: 'gemini:Kore | sharp, friendly co-host: asks what a smart listener would, pushes back with real objections, sometimes explains; dry wit, never exaggerated; brisk lively pace, never slow #ctx:1g5nl4j'
    '|a||Seven years later Anne Krueger gave the idea the name that stuck: rent seeking, spending real resources to win a transfer.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 8800
      voice: 'gemini:Achird | curious, open-minded economist host who loves a puzzle; warm, thinks aloud, brisk lively pace (never slow, never rushed); takes objections seriously, never preachy #ctx:19u31o2'
    '|a||Why is the rectangle exactly twice the triangle here? Show the math, or skip it?':
      mp3: 
      ms: 5960
      voice: gemini:Achird | curious, open-minded economist host who loves a puzzle; warm, thinks aloud, brisk lively pace (never slow, never rushed); takes objections seriously, never preachy
    '|a||With straight-line demand and a constant cost, a monopolist sells half the competitive quantity: eighty, not a hundred and sixty.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 8760
      voice: gemini:Achird | curious, open-minded economist host who loves a puzzle; warm, thinks aloud, brisk lively pace (never slow, never rushed); takes objections seriously, never preachy
    '|a||The rectangle is the markup times eighty. The triangle is half the markup times the eighty lost trips.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 7040
      voice: 'gemini:Achird | curious, open-minded economist host who loves a puzzle; warm, thinks aloud, brisk lively pace (never slow, never rushed); takes objections seriously, never preachy #ctx:g2s201'
    '|a||Same markup, same eighty, one with a half in front: the rectangle is always twice the triangle.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 6880
      voice: 'gemini:Achird | curious, open-minded economist host who loves a puzzle; warm, thinks aloud, brisk lively pace (never slow, never rushed); takes objections seriously, never preachy #ctx:hixfgf'
    '|a||So the rectangle is a prize, and a prize draws a fight. The open question is how much of it really goes up in smoke.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 8280
      voice: gemini:Achird | curious, open-minded economist host who loves a puzzle; warm, thinks aloud, brisk lively pace (never slow, never rushed); takes objections seriously, never preachy
    '|b||Here''s my objection. A full burn needs a race anyone can join. Many monopolies come from a patent, a lucky head start or a friend on the council, with no open race at all.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 11480
      voice: 'gemini:Kore | sharp, friendly co-host: asks what a smart listener would, pushes back with real objections, sometimes explains; dry wit, never exaggerated; brisk lively pace, never slow #ctx:llh3v'
    '|a||And where there is a race, it often looks cheap. Registered lobbying in Washington cost about four point four billion dollars in 2024, next to a federal budget near seven trillion.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 11760
      voice: 'gemini:Achird | curious, open-minded economist host who loves a puzzle; warm, thinks aloud, brisk lively pace (never slow, never rushed); takes objections seriously, never preachy #ctx:dlv65g'
    '|b||Tullock himself puzzled over why favours sell so cheaply. It''s known as the Tullock paradox.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 6320
      voice: 'gemini:Kore | sharp, friendly co-host: asks what a smart listener would, pushes back with real objections, sometimes explains; dry wit, never exaggerated; brisk lively pace, never slow #ctx:1v2pmyv'
    '|a||So the true cost lies somewhere between the triangle and the triangle plus the rectangle. Where depends on how open the fight is.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 8880
      voice: 'gemini:Achird | curious, open-minded economist host who loves a puzzle; warm, thinks aloud, brisk lively pace (never slow, never rushed); takes objections seriously, never preachy #ctx:f47l5k'
    '|b||How big, then, across a whole economy? Harberger said about a tenth of a percent of national income.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 6280
      voice: 'gemini:Kore | sharp, friendly co-host: asks what a smart listener would, pushes back with real objections, sometimes explains; dry wit, never exaggerated; brisk lively pace, never slow #ctx:840rl'
    '|a||In 1978 Keith Cowling and Dennis Mueller counted Tullock''s rectangles too, plus what large US firms spend on advertising to win market power. They got four to thirteen percent of those firms'' output.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 14080
      voice: 'gemini:Achird | curious, open-minded economist host who loves a puzzle; warm, thinks aloud, brisk lively pace (never slow, never rushed); takes objections seriously, never preachy #ctx:fr0fdq'
    '|b||So that the triangle is real is consensus. How big the full bill is, is still contested.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 6480
      voice: 'gemini:Kore | sharp, friendly co-host: asks what a smart listener would, pushes back with real objections, sometimes explains; dry wit, never exaggerated; brisk lively pace, never slow #ctx:fjcmp9'
    '|b||Three questions on new cases. Used up, or only moved? Sort each card.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 6200
      voice: 'gemini:Kore | sharp, friendly co-host: asks what a smart listener would, pushes back with real objections, sometimes explains; dry wit, never exaggerated; brisk lively pace, never slow #ctx:1poqrmn'
